From 7200638d93035c4a50174ab2c336766844373d4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Walter Dal Mut <walter.dalmut@corley.it>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 08:06:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/65] ARM: dts: rockchip: rk3506: Add the USB OTG0 controller

The RK3506 has two DWC2 USB 2.0 OTG controllers. Describe the first one,
the port that boards actually expose.

The compatible deliberately stops at the generic Rockchip string.
dwc2.yaml enumerates the SoC-specific compatibles it accepts and rk3506
is not among them, so a "rockchip,rk3506-usb" first entry would only make
dtbs_check fail; it can be added together with the binding change if a
per-SoC quirk ever turns out to be needed. "rockchip,rk3066-usb" is
already matched by the driver (drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c).

Only the "otg" clock is declared. The vendor dts also wires a "pmu" and
an "adp" clock, but dwc2.yaml allows just "otg" and "utmi", and mainline
dwc2 never touches the other two.

There is no "phys" property, because the RK3506 USB2 PHY is not supported
by phy-rockchip-inno-usb2 yet. dwc2 treats the PHY as optional: when
devm_phy_get() returns -ENODEV it leaves hsotg->phy NULL and carries on
(drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c). Whether the PHY comes out of reset in a
usable state is untested; if it does not, the node is still correct and
only needs the phys property added once the PHY driver knows this SoC.

Register base, interrupt and FIFO sizes are those of the vendor kernel
(rk3502.dtsi, from which the vendor rk3506 dtsi is built).

(cherry picked from commit 30c0c8aa69aa765007de174689c4c490ed0a9baa)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506.dtsi
index 4b923b5a8..5c1f5fa21 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3506.dtsi
@@ -223,6 +223,33 @@ ioc1: syscon@ff660000 {
 		reg = <0xff660000 0x10000>;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * OTG0, the USB port exposed on the board. No "phys" property: the
+	 * RK3506 USB2 PHY is not supported by phy-rockchip-inno-usb2 yet, and
+	 * dwc2 treats the PHY as optional (dwc2/platform.c, -ENODEV leaves
+	 * hsotg->phy NULL and the probe continues).
+	 *
+	 * Only the "otg" clock is declared: dwc2.yaml allows just "otg" and
+	 * "utmi", while the vendor also wires a "pmu" and an "adp" clock that
+	 * mainline never touches.
+	 *
+	 * The compatible omits a "rockchip,rk3506-usb" first entry on purpose:
+	 * dwc2.yaml enumerates the SoC-specific strings it accepts and rk3506
+	 * is not among them, so adding it here without the binding change
+	 * would only make dtbs_check fail.
+	 */
+	usb_otg0: usb@ff740000 {
+		compatible = "rockchip,rk3066-usb", "snps,dwc2";
+		reg = <0xff740000 0x40000>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 74 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		clocks = <&cru HCLK_USBOTG0>;
+		clock-names = "otg";
+		g-np-tx-fifo-size = <16>;
+		g-rx-fifo-size = <280>;
+		g-tx-fifo-size = <256 128 128 64 32 16>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * pinctrl "rockchip,rmio". Mandatory for this SoC:
 	 * pinctrl-rockchip.c returns -EINVAL when the phandle is missing,
